  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "A positive number \\(x\\) satisfies the inequality \\(\\sqrt x\\lt2x\\) if and only if",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x\\gt\\frac14\\)",
    "B": "\\(x\\gt2\\)",
    "C": "\\(x\\gt4\\)",
    "D": "\\(x\\lt\\frac14\\)",
    "E": "\\(x\\lt4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Because \\(x>0\\), both \\(\\sqrt{x}\\) and \\(2x\\) are positive. Squaring therefore preserves their order in both directions. We obtain\n\\[\n\\sqrt{x}<2x\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nx<4x^2.\n\\]\nDividing by the positive number \\(x\\), then by 4, gives\n\\[\n1<4x\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nx>\\frac14.\n\\]\nEvery step is reversible for positive \\(x\\). At \\(x=\\frac14\\), the original sides are equal, so the endpoint is excluded. The answer is \\(\\boxed{x>\\frac14}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
